1
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:41,959
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

2
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:48,048
ANY ADVICE FOR YOUNGER DESIGNERS
OR THOSE FINDING THEIR WAY?

3
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:51,969
DON'T TRY TOO HARD TO CHANGE YOURSELF
CHANGE WHERE YOU ARE

4
00:00:57,015 --> 00:00:58,016
Mr. Kang.

5
00:00:59,142 --> 00:01:00,143
Yes?

6
00:01:01,353 --> 00:01:02,354
What do you think

7
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:06,650
about me applying
for that expat position to Paris?

8
00:01:17,369 --> 00:01:18,704
I was just asking.

9
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:21,456
I'm already learning a lot right now

10
00:01:22,249 --> 00:01:25,460
but I was wondering what it'd be like
to be somewhere completely new.

11
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:30,882
I think it's a great idea.

12
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:36,179
- Do you mean it?
- Of course.

13
00:01:36,972 --> 00:01:39,266
It's important to learn
in a different environment.

14
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:43,770
And an employee's growth
is an advantage to the business.

15
00:01:45,272 --> 00:01:46,273
Give it a go.

16
00:01:50,193 --> 00:01:51,194
What about you?

17
00:01:52,237 --> 00:01:53,238
Me?

18
00:01:53,822 --> 00:01:54,823
Are you okay with it?

19
00:01:56,199 --> 00:01:57,200
Of course.

20
00:01:57,993 --> 00:02:00,537
The flight to Paris
isn't that long anyway.

21
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:12,591
What? Hey.

22
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:14,216
Why would you go there?

23
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:16,010
You just started dating
for the first time.

24
00:02:16,011 --> 00:02:17,012
What did he say?

25
00:02:17,346 --> 00:02:19,056
What do you think?
He must be shocked and scared.

26
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:20,641
He said he's fine with it.

27
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:22,517
- What?
- What?

28
00:02:24,102 --> 00:02:26,062
He told me to go to Paris.

29
00:02:26,063 --> 00:02:28,231
Wait, maybe he was too flustered.

30
00:02:28,982 --> 00:02:30,108
He seemed to mean it.

31
00:02:31,443 --> 00:02:33,403
Hey, let me tell you this
because I've been there.

32
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:36,239
Long-distance relationships
never work out.

33
00:02:37,282 --> 00:02:39,242
- Why?
- Your boyfriend

34
00:02:39,451 --> 00:02:41,535
is someone even CEO Han Jeong-yeon
wanted to date.

35
00:02:41,536 --> 00:02:43,622
Women won't let him be alone
during that long period.

36
00:02:44,039 --> 00:02:45,539
- They'll snatch him right away.
- What?

37
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:47,833
Yes, you said there were
more than a couple of women

38
00:02:47,834 --> 00:02:49,378
who asked him out at work.

39
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:52,046
LET'S SNATCH KANG HA-GI RIGHT AWAY

40
00:02:52,047 --> 00:02:54,048
- Kang Ha-gi!
- Kang Ha-gi!

41
00:02:54,049 --> 00:02:55,174
No way.

42
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:57,177
No matter how I think about it,
it can't happen.

43
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:17,030
I love you, Da-reum.

44
00:03:17,906 --> 00:03:19,116
I love you, too.

45
00:03:26,498 --> 00:03:27,624
- Hey!
- My goodness!

46
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:29,209
What's taking you so long?

47
00:03:29,751 --> 00:03:30,960
I'm hungry.

48
00:03:30,961 --> 00:03:33,295
You've been
frying those dumplings all day long.

49
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:34,339
Why, that...

50
00:03:43,807 --> 00:03:45,100
Yes.

51
00:03:47,269 --> 00:03:49,813
Wow, you've burned them all.

52
00:03:50,731 --> 00:03:54,109
So why did you tell her to go
if you didn't even mean it?

53
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:57,404
It's so hot.

54
00:04:00,699 --> 00:04:01,782
Listen up.

55
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:02,826
Dating is like a fried dumpling.

56
00:04:03,994 --> 00:04:05,536
When it gets hot, flip it over.

57
00:04:05,537 --> 00:04:07,122
When you want to cool it,
put it down.

58
00:04:07,497 --> 00:04:10,584
You need a bit of distance
to stay together even longer.

59
00:04:11,042 --> 00:04:13,169
You're taking a step back
to take two steps forward later.

60
00:04:13,170 --> 00:04:15,464
That's what real players do.

61
00:04:20,594 --> 00:04:22,345
Why did it have to be France?

62
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:26,099
People there greet each other
with a kiss on the cheek.

63
00:04:27,309 --> 00:04:29,394
- I don't like it.
- Are you anxious already?

64
00:04:30,771 --> 00:04:32,980
- I'm not.
- You're scared.

65
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:36,276
Just be cool and let Da-reum go.
Don't be so lame.

66
00:04:37,027 --> 00:04:39,738
If you go, that'll be the end of it.
You two will break up for sure.

67
00:04:40,155 --> 00:04:41,614
Let her go
so you can be together longer.

68
00:04:41,615 --> 00:04:43,365
Be cool about it and let her go.
It's a go!

69
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:45,118
You cannot go. It's a no!

70
00:04:46,203 --> 00:04:49,915
- Go!
- No!

71
00:04:53,877 --> 00:04:55,669
FINAL EPISODE

72
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:56,838
CEO KANG HA-GI

73
00:05:04,971 --> 00:05:06,139
Come in.

74
00:05:07,432 --> 00:05:08,517
Mr. Kang.

75
00:05:09,351 --> 00:05:11,353
Have you seen the notice
HAN sent today?

76
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:13,396
No, not yet.

77
00:05:13,814 --> 00:05:15,941
It was about our expat employee.

78
00:05:16,608 --> 00:05:20,445
"If possible, we'd like to have
Ms. Nam Da-reum sent here."

79
00:05:21,029 --> 00:05:22,280
That's what it says.

80
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:28,077
REQUESTING EXPAT EMPLOYEE FROM KOREA

81
00:05:28,078 --> 00:05:29,370
STATIONED AT:
MAISON HAN PARIS HEADQUARTERS

82
00:05:29,371 --> 00:05:30,497
REQUESTED EMPLOYEE:
NAM DA-REUM

83
00:05:31,206 --> 00:05:33,250
I haven't checked
with Ms. Da-reum yet.

84
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:36,628
- Please do.
- Sorry?

85
00:05:37,546 --> 00:05:40,130
Tell them that we'll consider
the request favorably

86
00:05:40,131 --> 00:05:41,716
if she wishes to go.

87
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:45,887
- Favorably?
- Yes.

88
00:05:46,346 --> 00:05:47,389
It's a great opportunity.

89
00:05:47,848 --> 00:05:49,975
The employee's growth leads
to the company's growth.

90
00:05:51,393 --> 00:05:52,601
It's growth for everyone.

91
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:54,437
GROWTH FOR EVERYONE

92
00:05:57,274 --> 00:05:58,608
Mr. Kang.

93
00:05:59,025 --> 00:06:02,279
- Are you sure about this?
- Yes, of course.

94
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:06,241
All right, then.

95
00:06:31,433 --> 00:06:32,434
KIM MIN-WOO

96
00:06:32,726 --> 00:06:35,353
Hey, I just saw
Mr. Choi Seong-wook here.

97
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:43,319
HAND CAR WASH

98
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:45,237
It'll take you forever
to wash all three cars.

99
00:06:45,238 --> 00:06:46,531
Move it, will you?

100
00:06:46,907 --> 00:06:48,198
Did you get this part?

101
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:51,119
You didn't get the wheels.
Get to it already.

102
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:53,704
- Choi.
- Yes?

103
00:06:53,705 --> 00:06:55,956
Don't just wipe the sides.
Get the roof too.

104
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:57,250
Yes, sir.

105
00:06:58,543 --> 00:07:02,547
- Don't slack off. Wipe it harder.
- Yes, sir.

106
00:07:37,415 --> 00:07:38,625
You left to do this job?

107
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,627
Why did you do it
when you didn't even make a big haul?

108
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:44,297
Right? Tell me about it.

109
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:51,805
Why didn't you send them

110
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:53,515
the final version?

111
00:07:58,728 --> 00:07:59,813
Because I'm an idiot.

112
00:08:07,654 --> 00:08:08,822
I couldn't bear

113
00:08:09,531 --> 00:08:10,907
to see you go down.

114
00:08:15,704 --> 00:08:16,705
Do you remember?

115
00:08:17,789 --> 00:08:21,501
When we first got
an office for Appello

116
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:24,337
we carried boxes
all throughout the night.

117
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:26,964
Whenever the server crashed

118
00:08:26,965 --> 00:08:28,925
we'd spend days
practically living there.

119
00:08:30,593 --> 00:08:31,720
So how could I

120
00:08:33,054 --> 00:08:34,431
forget all that?

121
00:08:38,935 --> 00:08:41,688
I got some relief
after doing that awful thing.

122
00:08:43,398 --> 00:08:45,191
But my heart hit rock bottom.

123
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:47,610
I didn't know what got into me.

124
00:08:51,281 --> 00:08:52,574
This is for the better.

125
00:08:56,244 --> 00:08:57,454
No one's going to understand that.

126
00:08:59,039 --> 00:09:00,957
You should've stabbed my back
and gotten good money for it.

127
00:09:02,417 --> 00:09:03,501
I still...

128
00:09:07,130 --> 00:09:08,506
despise you so much.

129
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:14,471
Yes, that's only fair.

130
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:22,854
Ha-gi.

131
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:26,316
It's not your fault

132
00:09:27,484 --> 00:09:30,361
that I've become broken.
It's not because you succeeded.

133
00:09:32,322 --> 00:09:33,323
It's just that...

134
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:40,497
Instead of cheering you on

135
00:09:42,457 --> 00:09:45,210
I hated myself for feeling so petty.

136
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:50,090
And I couldn't deal with it.

137
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:59,015
I'm sorry. I mean it.

138
00:10:03,228 --> 00:10:04,521
And thanks

139
00:10:05,188 --> 00:10:08,525
for giving me a chance
to make an excuse.

140
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:15,323
Hey, Choi. We're busy over here!

141
00:10:15,949 --> 00:10:17,033
Yes, coming!

142
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:26,417
Hey, Ha-gi.

143
00:10:29,045 --> 00:10:30,213
I'll always be...

144
00:10:31,798 --> 00:10:33,633
grateful for you, man.

145
00:10:37,011 --> 00:10:38,054
I have to go.

146
00:11:05,832 --> 00:11:07,499
OVERSEAS ASSIGNMENT APPLICATION

147
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,169
ASSIGNED TO:
MAISON HAN PARIS HEADQUARTERS

148
00:11:14,924 --> 00:11:16,384
I thought you'd be thrilled.

149
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:21,973
What's wrong? Is it Mr. Kang?

150
00:11:30,023 --> 00:11:32,567
He's already having a tough time
because of Mr. Choi.

151
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:35,320
I didn't want to add to that.

152
00:11:38,156 --> 00:11:40,867
Well, I guess
the timing is a bit off.

153
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:42,785
Will you be okay...

154
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:46,247
giving up on this?

155
00:11:51,377 --> 00:11:56,132
You should give serious thought
about what you really want.

156
00:12:13,358 --> 00:12:14,734
Seong-wook said

157
00:12:15,652 --> 00:12:17,194
he hated himself
for having awful feelings

158
00:12:17,195 --> 00:12:19,197
for someone
he should be showing support to.

159
00:12:22,951 --> 00:12:24,118
It hit close to home.

160
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:29,540
I know it's a great opportunity
for Ms. Da-reum.

161
00:12:32,961 --> 00:12:34,379
But I want her to stay.

162
00:12:37,632 --> 00:12:38,841
I find myself so pathetic.

163
00:12:42,512 --> 00:12:44,222
By now, I should be
used to saying goodbye...

164
00:12:48,685 --> 00:12:50,228
to people.

165
00:12:52,772 --> 00:12:54,107
But it's too hard.

166
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:59,862
Then cling to her.

167
00:13:00,905 --> 00:13:02,030
Okay?

168
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:03,783
If I did that
because I couldn't handle it

169
00:13:04,826 --> 00:13:06,619
it would kill her dream too.

170
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:12,000
I should let her go.

171
00:13:17,797 --> 00:13:18,965
That's the right thing to do.

172
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:25,346
I really can't deal with you.

173
00:13:35,315 --> 00:13:36,983
Hey, be careful.

174
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:39,860
Hey, man. Pull it together.

175
00:13:39,861 --> 00:13:41,654
Kang Ha-gi.

176
00:13:42,030 --> 00:13:43,656
Hey, I'm fine.

177
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:45,199
I'm totally fine.

178
00:13:45,742 --> 00:13:46,826
Let's go for round two.

179
00:13:47,618 --> 00:13:48,745
To my place!

180
00:13:49,996 --> 00:13:52,247
You have to give her
your drunken honesty

181
00:13:52,248 --> 00:13:53,916
- instead of looking wasted.
- Excellent.

182
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:56,669
On my way.

183
00:13:57,045 --> 00:13:58,879
- My drunken confession!
- Okay.

184
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:00,465
- On my way!
- Mr. Kang.

185
00:14:00,798 --> 00:14:01,883
Mr. Kang.

186
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:09,724
- Are you okay?
- It's Ms. Da-reum.

187
00:14:10,183 --> 00:14:11,267
It's me.

188
00:14:11,809 --> 00:14:13,603
- Ms. Da-reum.
- Yes?

189
00:14:13,728 --> 00:14:14,771
Ms. Da-reum.

190
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:19,400
You're so cute.

191
00:14:21,903 --> 00:14:23,988
You're way too cute, my dear Da-reum.

192
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:28,201
So you're drunk.

193
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:32,914
How do I let you go
when you're so cute?

194
00:14:36,459 --> 00:14:37,585
Kiss me.

195
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:42,381
Have you lost your mind?

196
00:14:42,382 --> 00:14:43,757
Go do that at home.

197
00:14:43,758 --> 00:14:45,134
Mr. Kang.

198
00:14:45,343 --> 00:14:46,802
Are you okay?

199
00:14:46,803 --> 00:14:48,554
I've never seen him so wasted before.

200
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:52,849
Let's take him back home for now.

201
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:54,685
- One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

202
00:14:55,645 --> 00:14:58,230
- Are you okay?
- Someone hit me.

203
00:14:58,231 --> 00:15:00,066
- No one did. Let's go.
- No.

204
00:15:01,526 --> 00:15:03,111
Why did you drink so much?

205
00:15:03,653 --> 00:15:04,821
You can go too.

206
00:15:05,071 --> 00:15:08,282
- I'm fine, really.
- Where are you telling me to go?

207
00:15:09,534 --> 00:15:10,952
Sit down for a minute.

208
00:15:31,597 --> 00:15:32,598
Mr. Kang?

209
00:15:33,891 --> 00:15:34,892
Mr. Kang.

210
00:15:49,157 --> 00:15:50,575
Don't go.

211
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:00,501
Don't go, Da-reum.

212
00:16:26,777 --> 00:16:28,905
He's not cool with it.

213
00:16:30,031 --> 00:16:32,825
He just doesn't want
to get in your way.

214
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:08,402
CONTACT SOLUTION, Q-TIPS

215
00:17:09,195 --> 00:17:11,989
TRAVEL PILLOW, BLANKET,
PAIN RELIEF PATCHES, RAMYEON

216
00:17:23,417 --> 00:17:25,001
OUR BELOVED
PARIS, FRANCE

217
00:17:25,002 --> 00:17:26,586
SUPPLIES FOR PARIS

218
00:17:26,587 --> 00:17:27,964
BAND-AID, OINTMENT, INSTANT SOUP

219
00:17:51,862 --> 00:17:53,613
Should we do these

220
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:56,158
for Olivier's new colors?

221
00:17:57,285 --> 00:17:58,785
It's too light.

222
00:17:58,786 --> 00:18:00,704
Wasn't there a jacket?

223
00:18:00,705 --> 00:18:01,706
Like this one.

224
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:05,083
Ms. Da-reum took the day off.

225
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:08,170
Today was the deadline to apply
to work abroad, and she didn't apply.

226
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:27,690
SPICY CHICKEN, ANGUK BRANCH
8,530 WON, ACCEPT

227
00:18:44,665 --> 00:18:46,709
QUICK DELIVERY

228
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:54,215
ONE, TWO, THREE, FOUR, FIVE
LET'S GO

229
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:59,012
- D.N.X.
- D.N.X.

230
00:18:59,013 --> 00:19:00,263
MUSIC WAVE

231
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:04,352
- D.N.X.
- D.N.X.

232
00:19:08,189 --> 00:19:09,690
- One.
- Two.

233
00:19:09,899 --> 00:19:11,399
- Three.
- Four.

234
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:13,151
Five. Let's go!

235
00:19:13,152 --> 00:19:14,570
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

236
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:24,871
ONE, TWO,
THREE, FOUR

237
00:19:24,872 --> 00:19:27,750
FIVE, LET'S GO

238
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:47,186
I feel so much more relieved
after deciding not to go.

239
00:19:54,443 --> 00:19:57,071
I mean, Paris isn't a big deal.

240
00:19:57,446 --> 00:20:00,366
Here, I got my friends, Appello...

241
00:20:01,826 --> 00:20:03,703
No matter how hard things get

242
00:20:04,912 --> 00:20:06,038
don't let go of my hand.

243
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:09,583
Okay.

244
00:20:12,878 --> 00:20:14,213
...and Mr. Kang.

245
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:19,343
Okay, Nam Da-reum.

246
00:20:20,052 --> 00:20:21,137
You made a great decision.

247
00:20:30,354 --> 00:20:31,355
How sweet.

248
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:01,927
You're alive.

249
00:21:06,182 --> 00:21:07,224
Chan.

250
00:21:12,855 --> 00:21:14,857
I should've been there by your side.

251
00:21:16,066 --> 00:21:17,151
I'm sorry.

252
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:19,695
Why are you apologizing?

253
00:21:22,698 --> 00:21:23,908
I let go of your hand.

254
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:27,578
You didn't.

255
00:21:28,746 --> 00:21:29,997
I'm the one who ran away.

256
00:21:37,046 --> 00:21:40,382
Jeez. You must've been
the most frightened.

257
00:21:41,217 --> 00:21:43,928
But I must've been young too
because I ran away like you.

258
00:21:48,724 --> 00:21:49,725
Let us...

259
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:52,937
stop running away.

260
00:21:55,523 --> 00:21:56,607
Come back, Roy.

261
00:22:01,111 --> 00:22:03,656
Do you think
the other guys will accept me?

262
00:22:08,077 --> 00:22:11,580
They talk crap about you
when your part comes on at practice.

263
00:22:12,748 --> 00:22:14,667
They pretend like
they hate you so much

264
00:22:15,209 --> 00:22:16,252
yet they wait.

265
00:22:20,881 --> 00:22:21,924
Did you see the ad?

266
00:22:22,925 --> 00:22:24,593
That's how we all feel.

267
00:22:48,325 --> 00:22:49,660
CEO KANG HA-GI OF APPELLO

268
00:22:51,328 --> 00:22:53,080
You know the application
is due today, right?

269
00:22:53,706 --> 00:22:55,040
I'll wait until you come.

270
00:23:09,722 --> 00:23:12,599
YOU KNOW THE APPLICATION
IS DUE TODAY, RIGHT?

271
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:13,726
I'LL WAIT UNTIL YOU COME

272
00:23:47,176 --> 00:23:48,177
Ms. Da-reum.

273
00:23:49,595 --> 00:23:50,888
Have you really been waiting for me?

274
00:23:52,514 --> 00:23:53,515
Yes.

275
00:23:58,771 --> 00:24:00,105
You didn't turn in the application...

276
00:24:02,107 --> 00:24:03,609
and you made me worry all day.

277
00:24:06,070 --> 00:24:09,281
You kept pretending
like you were cool with it too.

278
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:11,200
Did you think I wouldn't notice?

279
00:24:11,700 --> 00:24:13,369
I'm the expert at acting fine.

280
00:24:15,412 --> 00:24:16,914
Is that why you ran away?

281
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:22,294
No.

282
00:24:25,047 --> 00:24:27,424
Working with you

283
00:24:28,050 --> 00:24:29,259
eating with you

284
00:24:29,969 --> 00:24:32,596
and staying by your side
on days when we have nothing to do

285
00:24:33,764 --> 00:24:35,265
were what I loved.

286
00:24:39,853 --> 00:24:42,106
So I wanted to keep being with you.

287
00:24:44,566 --> 00:24:45,567
Ms. Da-reum.

288
00:24:46,068 --> 00:24:47,778
If I must choose one or the other...

289
00:24:50,030 --> 00:24:51,156
I choose you.

290
00:25:04,086 --> 00:25:05,170
You're right.

291
00:25:05,879 --> 00:25:07,548
I didn't want you to go.

292
00:25:11,260 --> 00:25:13,178
I thought this could mean
goodbye forever

293
00:25:14,430 --> 00:25:15,514
so I got anxious.

294
00:25:17,725 --> 00:25:19,143
But what beat my anxiety...

295
00:25:23,313 --> 00:25:25,357
must be my love for you.

296
00:25:27,026 --> 00:25:28,360
What I hated more was the idea

297
00:25:29,236 --> 00:25:30,279
of you not going because of me.

298
00:25:34,908 --> 00:25:36,160
When you talked about Paris

299
00:25:37,911 --> 00:25:39,663
your eyes dazzled so brightly.

300
00:25:42,041 --> 00:25:43,667
It was the face...

301
00:25:46,086 --> 00:25:47,337
I fell in love with.

302
00:25:48,964 --> 00:25:50,007
A face full of excitement

303
00:25:50,674 --> 00:25:51,800
and happiness.

304
00:25:53,385 --> 00:25:54,762
I hope to see you...

305
00:25:57,139 --> 00:25:59,183
always looking like that.

306
00:26:07,316 --> 00:26:08,901
Don't worry about me and go.

307
00:26:09,860 --> 00:26:10,903
See and experience

308
00:26:12,029 --> 00:26:13,113
as much as you can.

309
00:26:17,117 --> 00:26:18,660
So that you can do an even better job

310
00:26:19,536 --> 00:26:21,997
at what you want to do, okay?

311
00:26:28,295 --> 00:26:29,546
Even if I leave...

312
00:26:33,217 --> 00:26:34,968
you won't let go, will you?

313
00:26:37,679 --> 00:26:38,847
Of course not.

314
00:26:40,140 --> 00:26:41,558
We'd be holding each other
more tightly.

315
00:26:45,312 --> 00:26:46,313
Let us

316
00:26:46,980 --> 00:26:48,107
trust each other.

317
00:26:54,488 --> 00:26:55,531
Okay?

318
00:27:18,679 --> 00:27:20,346
Congratulations, Da-reum.

319
00:27:20,347 --> 00:27:22,641
I mean, Paris? That's so cool.

320
00:27:23,308 --> 00:27:25,268
Upload lots of pictures
in the group chat, okay?

321
00:27:25,269 --> 00:27:27,228
And you have to come back.

322
00:27:27,229 --> 00:27:29,647
Yes, I'll make sure
I check in with you.

323
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:31,524
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

324
00:27:31,525 --> 00:27:33,901
Wait, you can't do that without me.
Let me do it too.

325
00:27:33,902 --> 00:27:37,531
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

326
00:27:42,161 --> 00:27:43,453
Are you ready to go?

327
00:27:43,912 --> 00:27:46,957
I have something to share with you.

328
00:27:52,629 --> 00:27:55,174
Oh my gosh. Mr. Kang.

329
00:27:57,301 --> 00:27:58,302
Actually...

330
00:28:00,512 --> 00:28:01,638
Ms. Da-reum and I are...

331
00:28:02,556 --> 00:28:03,807
We know, Mr. Kang.

332
00:28:06,685 --> 00:28:08,769
Wow, congratulations.

333
00:28:08,770 --> 00:28:10,271
- Congrats.
- Good for you.

334
00:28:10,272 --> 00:28:11,690
- Finally.
- It was about time.

335
00:28:14,568 --> 00:28:17,236
I wasn't done talking.

336
00:28:17,237 --> 00:28:20,699
Do you know how tiring it was
to pretend like we didn't know?

337
00:28:20,824 --> 00:28:24,911
- Tell me about it. It was tiring.
- So exhausting.

338
00:28:24,912 --> 00:28:26,622
It was fun to see your awful acting.

339
00:28:31,919 --> 00:28:34,545
We won't be able to hold
the rookies' meet-up for a while.

340
00:28:34,546 --> 00:28:35,713
Right?

341
00:28:35,714 --> 00:28:38,800
It was mostly the two of us, anyway.

342
00:28:40,886 --> 00:28:42,387
I need cola.

343
00:28:43,138 --> 00:28:45,140
Hey, give me some soda.

344
00:28:45,849 --> 00:28:47,058
That wrong message in the chat...

345
00:28:47,059 --> 00:28:48,352
Mr. Kang.

346
00:28:55,275 --> 00:28:57,318
- One, two, three, four.
- One, two, three, four.

347
00:28:57,319 --> 00:28:59,278
- Five, six, seven, eight.
- Five, six, seven, eight.

348
00:28:59,279 --> 00:29:01,697
- Two, two, three, four...
- Wait.

349
00:29:01,698 --> 00:29:04,075
Chan, you stepped out
half a beat too early.

350
00:29:04,076 --> 00:29:06,994
No, I stepped out at "two, two."
You got out at "two."

351
00:29:06,995 --> 00:29:08,204
You were both rushing.

352
00:29:08,205 --> 00:29:10,331
- Hey.
- You were both wrong, so get back.

353
00:29:10,332 --> 00:29:12,833
- Hey, Teo.
- Fine. I was wrong. Do it over.

354
00:29:12,834 --> 00:29:15,462
You know how it goes.
This isn't it. Hurry up.

355
00:29:20,676 --> 00:29:21,677
You're here.

356
00:29:28,517 --> 00:29:30,435
I'm a bit late, aren't I?

357
00:29:41,071 --> 00:29:42,698
I've been waiting for so long.

358
00:29:49,871 --> 00:29:52,164
- I missed you, kid.
- Me too.

359
00:29:52,165 --> 00:29:54,792
- Let me see our baby's face.
- Have you all been well?

360
00:29:54,793 --> 00:29:57,128
What did you go through?
You're a mess for a K-pop idol.

361
00:29:57,129 --> 00:29:59,046
- You're right.
- He looks way better than you guys.

362
00:29:59,047 --> 00:30:00,424
What are you talking about?

363
00:30:11,143 --> 00:30:12,728
- What took you so long?
- What took you so long?

364
00:30:15,147 --> 00:30:18,400
APPELLO CLOSED
COLLEGEIST POP-UP IS OVER, THANK YOU

365
00:30:43,508 --> 00:30:44,885
Can you play this song?

366
00:31:01,026 --> 00:31:02,778
YOU
DEMO VERSION

367
00:31:08,742 --> 00:31:09,743
What do you think?

368
00:31:12,496 --> 00:31:13,497
I love it.

369
00:31:15,499 --> 00:31:16,541
That's it?

370
00:31:21,129 --> 00:31:22,130
It feels weird.

371
00:31:23,340 --> 00:31:25,092
You may be saying it to your fans

372
00:31:25,759 --> 00:31:28,303
but it's what I wanted to say to you.

373
00:31:32,557 --> 00:31:33,642
So you're saying

374
00:31:35,018 --> 00:31:36,144
it's a pass?

375
00:31:47,406 --> 00:31:49,741
We both held out
for quite a long time.

376
00:31:52,994 --> 00:31:54,704
Hey, that's...

377
00:31:59,292 --> 00:32:03,045
This is the exact shape
that my all-time favorite celebrity

378
00:32:03,046 --> 00:32:04,756
always draws
when he signs autographs.

379
00:32:04,965 --> 00:32:06,799
Today is my birthday

380
00:32:06,800 --> 00:32:08,593
so I want to buy it for myself
as a gift.

381
00:32:08,844 --> 00:32:11,179
Excuse me. Happy birthday.

382
00:32:16,435 --> 00:32:17,519
It was me.

383
00:32:18,270 --> 00:32:19,980
I gave you that pendant
on your birthday.

384
00:32:25,026 --> 00:32:26,903
And because you had kept it all along

385
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:29,781
I found the courage
to get back on stage.

386
00:32:33,785 --> 00:32:36,705
I also endured life,
believing that it was from you.

387
00:32:44,296 --> 00:32:45,338
I think...

388
00:32:47,174 --> 00:32:50,677
I figured out
what it is that I want to do.

389
00:32:51,928 --> 00:32:54,139
Just as I was happy as your fan

390
00:32:54,389 --> 00:32:58,143
I also want to do something
that'll awaken passion

391
00:32:58,810 --> 00:32:59,895
in people's hearts.

392
00:33:05,025 --> 00:33:06,443
Is that why you're going to Paris?

393
00:33:08,820 --> 00:33:09,863
Yes.

394
00:33:10,947 --> 00:33:12,491
I don't know
if I can pull it off, though.

395
00:33:13,241 --> 00:33:14,493
I'm sure you will.

396
00:33:15,410 --> 00:33:18,371
I've seen
how serious you are about this.

397
00:33:23,335 --> 00:33:26,213
I was happy to have someone
so wonderful as my fan.

398
00:33:31,718 --> 00:33:32,761
Now, it's your turn

399
00:33:33,929 --> 00:33:35,055
to do what makes your heart race.

400
00:33:53,573 --> 00:33:54,616
Passport.

401
00:33:55,033 --> 00:33:56,034
Here.

402
00:33:56,952 --> 00:33:57,953
The guidebook.

403
00:33:58,828 --> 00:33:59,871
Here.

404
00:34:00,914 --> 00:34:01,957
Emergency medicine.

405
00:34:04,209 --> 00:34:06,211
You basically bought me a pharmacy.

406
00:34:08,505 --> 00:34:09,839
Are you sure it's enough?

407
00:34:11,967 --> 00:34:13,301
I'm not going to Paris
to sell medicine.

408
00:34:13,927 --> 00:34:15,262
I just don't want you to get sick.

409
00:34:19,349 --> 00:34:21,726
I think I got everything, right?

410
00:34:31,403 --> 00:34:32,654
That's our knot.

411
00:34:33,280 --> 00:34:34,531
You attached it there.

412
00:34:37,784 --> 00:34:39,286
I'm taking this with me.

413
00:34:39,619 --> 00:34:41,371
So it'll feel like
we're still together.

414
00:34:52,299 --> 00:34:53,383
Are you touched?

415
00:34:56,678 --> 00:34:58,513
- A little.
- Only a little?

416
00:35:01,224 --> 00:35:02,225
Actually, a lot.

417
00:35:08,148 --> 00:35:09,983
Maybe I should leave
something behind too.

418
00:35:11,526 --> 00:35:12,527
Like what?

419
00:35:14,029 --> 00:35:15,947
It's a secret. I'll tell you later.

420
00:35:30,378 --> 00:35:31,713
I'll be back soon.

421
00:35:34,007 --> 00:35:35,342
I'll be waiting.

422
00:35:58,239 --> 00:36:01,368
DA-REUM HEART HA-GI

423
00:36:04,579 --> 00:36:07,916
6 MONTHS LATER

424
00:36:09,709 --> 00:36:11,168
Da-reum.

425
00:36:11,169 --> 00:36:13,129
The CEO wants this version
by three o'clock.

426
00:36:13,755 --> 00:36:15,674
By three o'clock today?

427
00:36:16,091 --> 00:36:17,842
Yes, that's her style.

428
00:36:19,928 --> 00:36:21,846
She's obviously Korean.

429
00:36:22,305 --> 00:36:23,306
You can do it.

430
00:36:23,973 --> 00:36:25,016
Can you?

431
00:36:26,976 --> 00:36:29,062
- I can.
- Yes.

432
00:36:57,048 --> 00:36:58,174
HAN AND KOREA

433
00:37:08,560 --> 00:37:09,978
Finally.

434
00:37:53,813 --> 00:37:56,148
Ha-gi's mission while waiting.

435
00:37:56,149 --> 00:37:57,316
Sunlight.

436
00:37:57,317 --> 00:38:00,111
Water, then open the window
for some sunlight.

437
00:38:00,487 --> 00:38:02,864
When a new leaf grows,
send me a selfie with it.

438
00:38:03,323 --> 00:38:06,534
When a bud appears,
video call and show me.

439
00:38:47,867 --> 00:38:49,202
Bonjour.

440
00:38:50,870 --> 00:38:52,413
Are you at work on the weekend?

441
00:38:54,249 --> 00:38:55,458
Exactly.

442
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:58,502
Ms. Han is no joke.

443
00:38:58,503 --> 00:39:00,171
She bombards me with work.

444
00:39:00,588 --> 00:39:01,923
She's worse than you.

445
00:39:02,090 --> 00:39:04,050
But why do you look excited?

446
00:39:06,135 --> 00:39:08,429
It's tough, but it's still fun.

447
00:39:09,097 --> 00:39:10,640
If you're enjoying it
even though it's tough

448
00:39:11,099 --> 00:39:12,141
that means you're good at it.

449
00:39:14,602 --> 00:39:16,104
You sound like a CEO.

450
00:39:16,688 --> 00:39:17,772
Because I am one.

451
00:39:21,192 --> 00:39:23,444
How's work? Is everything okay?

452
00:39:23,695 --> 00:39:25,737
Oh, I found out just yesterday.

453
00:39:25,738 --> 00:39:27,531
Mr. Young-woo and Ms. Min-a
are going out.

454
00:39:27,532 --> 00:39:28,575
Really?

455
00:39:29,158 --> 00:39:31,743
Oh, I knew it.

456
00:39:31,744 --> 00:39:34,038
- Since when?
- Since last week.

457
00:39:34,664 --> 00:39:37,458
That's crazy. How did you know?

458
00:39:37,792 --> 00:39:39,252
It was obvious.

459
00:39:39,460 --> 00:39:40,795
Only those two think
it's still a secret.

460
00:39:43,631 --> 00:39:44,883
We were the same.

461
00:39:47,844 --> 00:39:49,762
Oh, right. Check this out.

462
00:39:51,180 --> 00:39:52,431
I think it's going to bloom soon.

463
00:39:52,432 --> 00:39:54,350
Oh, that's so pretty.

464
00:39:54,684 --> 00:39:56,643
How are you so good
at growing plants?

465
00:39:56,644 --> 00:39:58,062
I always end up killing them.

466
00:39:59,147 --> 00:40:00,398
- Are you grateful?
- Yes.

467
00:40:02,108 --> 00:40:03,192
Give me a reward.

468
00:40:11,743 --> 00:40:12,785
I miss you.

469
00:40:13,369 --> 00:40:14,370
I miss you too.

470
00:40:20,668 --> 00:40:23,003
Da-reum will come
to the concert on her own.

471
00:40:23,004 --> 00:40:24,297
You can ride with me.

472
00:40:25,214 --> 00:40:27,050
How's Seul-a going to get there?
Is she going alone?

473
00:40:27,675 --> 00:40:29,886
Or should I give her a ride too?

474
00:40:33,765 --> 00:40:34,766
Eyes on me.

475
00:40:35,391 --> 00:40:36,392
Eyes on you.

476
00:40:40,188 --> 00:40:41,272
Eyes on you.

477
00:40:41,689 --> 00:40:43,775
Thank you for calling Fan Goods Shop.

478
00:40:44,901 --> 00:40:46,819
Yes. The slogan?

479
00:40:47,487 --> 00:40:50,280
"Take my wallet, Hun-i."

480
00:40:50,281 --> 00:40:52,616
We're currently sold out.

481
00:40:52,617 --> 00:40:55,244
"Min-i stole my heart"
will be available tomorrow.

482
00:40:55,620 --> 00:40:57,372
You want 150? Okay.

483
00:40:57,580 --> 00:40:59,039
Okay. Thank you.

484
00:40:59,040 --> 00:41:00,667
Of course. It won't take long.

485
00:41:01,084 --> 00:41:02,085
Bye.

486
00:41:02,627 --> 00:41:04,252
One, two, three.

487
00:41:04,253 --> 00:41:05,922
One, two.

488
00:41:12,720 --> 00:41:15,390
- Okay.
- Nice. Good job.

489
00:41:23,356 --> 00:41:25,316
REUNION OF D.N.X
IN A FULL GROUP COMEBACK

490
00:41:28,277 --> 00:41:29,654
Oh, my gosh!

491
00:41:51,759 --> 00:41:54,303
Now, attention!

492
00:41:55,388 --> 00:41:56,472
You know what I'm going to do.

493
00:41:57,432 --> 00:41:59,142
It's time.

494
00:42:00,101 --> 00:42:01,102
Okay.

495
00:42:01,519 --> 00:42:04,439
There's something

496
00:42:04,689 --> 00:42:06,357
all new recruits must go through.

497
00:42:06,983 --> 00:42:08,943
Chae-yeon, are you

498
00:42:09,277 --> 00:42:12,237
Team Ha-gi or Team Chan?

499
00:42:12,238 --> 00:42:13,281
Or Team Jin-sang?

500
00:42:16,492 --> 00:42:19,620
- There must be at least one...
- Quiet.

501
00:42:21,372 --> 00:42:23,041
I'm on Team...

502
00:42:33,634 --> 00:42:34,677
Ha-gi.

503
00:42:39,307 --> 00:42:41,184
You should've chosen Team Jin-sang.

504
00:42:41,601 --> 00:42:44,270
She used to be on Team Ha-gi too.

505
00:42:45,313 --> 00:42:48,607
- I'm on Team Young-woo now.
- I'm on Team Min-a.

506
00:42:48,608 --> 00:42:50,525
Didn't I tell you not to flaunt
your office romance?

507
00:42:50,526 --> 00:42:51,694
Stop it.

508
00:42:52,070 --> 00:42:55,448
By the way, is Mr. Kang single?

509
00:43:00,203 --> 00:43:01,453
Yes.

510
00:43:01,454 --> 00:43:04,499
Separate the preferred brand data
for North America and Europe.

511
00:43:22,725 --> 00:43:26,104
It looks like he's doing nothing,
but working.

512
00:43:26,854 --> 00:43:27,897
Okay.

513
00:43:28,773 --> 00:43:30,232
Do you want me to tell you?

514
00:43:30,233 --> 00:43:33,069
Whether Mr. Kang is
in a relationship or not?

515
00:43:34,862 --> 00:43:36,572
Oh, I'm sorry.

516
00:43:37,865 --> 00:43:40,409
- I knew it.
- Too bad.

517
00:43:41,035 --> 00:43:42,120
He already has a girlfriend.

518
00:43:45,039 --> 00:43:46,624
Da-reum!

519
00:43:48,459 --> 00:43:51,212
I, Nam Da-reum, just landed.

520
00:43:57,426 --> 00:43:58,678
Really?

521
00:44:11,399 --> 00:44:13,818
Welcome back. When did you come back?

522
00:44:18,656 --> 00:44:19,699
I thought you were coming tomorrow.

523
00:44:20,491 --> 00:44:21,576
I moved it up a day.

524
00:44:23,035 --> 00:44:24,036
Why?

525
00:44:26,539 --> 00:44:27,540
Because I missed you.

526
00:44:56,569 --> 00:44:58,154
I'm finally home.

527
00:45:02,909 --> 00:45:04,202
There's something
we haven't done yet.

528
00:45:19,634 --> 00:45:21,010
This is it.

529
00:45:23,721 --> 00:45:25,723
The reason I wanted to be back.

530
00:45:47,078 --> 00:45:49,454
The manager in charge will
suggest the merchandise

531
00:45:49,455 --> 00:45:51,332
in time for your comeback.

532
00:45:51,707 --> 00:45:53,042
Who's the new manager?

533
00:45:57,880 --> 00:45:59,214
Hello.

534
00:45:59,215 --> 00:46:01,467
- Hello.
- Hello.

535
00:46:04,720 --> 00:46:08,431
I'm your D.N.X collaboration
project manager, Nam Da-reum.

536
00:46:08,432 --> 00:46:09,600
Nice to meet you.

537
00:46:13,020 --> 00:46:15,064
We're honored to have you.

538
00:46:15,690 --> 00:46:17,233
Then let me begin.

539
00:46:18,818 --> 00:46:22,237
Your fan song "YOU" is the motive
of this collaboration.

540
00:46:22,238 --> 00:46:24,739
I reflected your gratitude
to your fans for waiting so long

541
00:46:24,740 --> 00:46:26,284
in the merchandise.

542
00:46:26,659 --> 00:46:30,036
As you can see,
I prepared three items.

543
00:46:30,037 --> 00:46:31,998
A T-shirt, a tote bag, and a cap.

544
00:46:32,331 --> 00:46:35,209
You can see the details
on the T-shirt.

545
00:46:35,418 --> 00:46:38,336
The pocket on the left
that's close to the heart is

546
00:46:38,337 --> 00:46:42,049
embroidered with lyrics from "YOU."

547
00:46:42,258 --> 00:46:43,718
That was good.

548
00:46:46,095 --> 00:46:47,220
That was cool.

549
00:46:47,221 --> 00:46:49,557
Oh, you're teasing me.

550
00:46:50,099 --> 00:46:51,309
I mean it.

551
00:46:52,560 --> 00:46:54,228
We're working together for real now.

552
00:46:54,979 --> 00:46:56,397
So I'd better pull this off.

553
00:46:56,981 --> 00:46:59,150
I'm not going to handle this project
as a fan.

554
00:46:59,442 --> 00:47:02,193
- Then?
- As a manager

555
00:47:02,194 --> 00:47:03,487
who understands the fans.

556
00:47:05,406 --> 00:47:06,866
I look forward to working with you

557
00:47:07,366 --> 00:47:09,076
Manager Nam Da-reum.

558
00:47:13,831 --> 00:47:17,501
- Likewise, Artist Lee Chan.
- Thank you.

559
00:47:20,504 --> 00:47:22,006
Good luck.

560
00:47:30,681 --> 00:47:32,683
That was a good briefing.

561
00:47:34,477 --> 00:47:37,313
- Did you hear it?
- I could hear your voice outside.

562
00:47:37,813 --> 00:47:39,065
You sounded pretty confident.

563
00:47:40,483 --> 00:47:42,109
I can leave you
with an even bigger project now.

564
00:47:43,444 --> 00:47:45,905
Are you complimenting me,
so you can make me work overtime?

565
00:47:46,947 --> 00:47:47,990
Not today.

566
00:47:49,158 --> 00:47:51,577
- Why not?
- I have a date with my boyfriend.

567
00:48:06,384 --> 00:48:07,717
THROUGH ALL TIME AND SPACE

568
00:48:07,718 --> 00:48:09,470
For the lyrics,
the fans will like this...

569
00:48:12,014 --> 00:48:13,765
and this the most.

570
00:48:13,766 --> 00:48:14,850
Okay, Ms. Da-reum.

571
00:48:15,351 --> 00:48:16,811
Then...

572
00:48:17,770 --> 00:48:19,522
Is this right?

573
00:48:21,315 --> 00:48:22,316
That's perfect.

574
00:48:25,444 --> 00:48:27,113
D.N.X CONCERT ATTIRE REFERENCE DESIGN

575
00:48:31,242 --> 00:48:32,784
CHECK COMEBACK SHOWCASE SPONSOR BOOTH

576
00:48:32,785 --> 00:48:34,662
CONFIRM STAGE OUTFIT KEY MERCHANDISE

577
00:48:34,870 --> 00:48:36,664
